sections.body:
- `src/slicer/relayrun.py`:
  - `append` takes the target path and never calls `feedback.ensure_gitignore` for a fallback write;
  - `fold` takes events from several files, ordered by `at` with a stable tie-break of file order then line, and drops an event identical to one already folded;
  - `list_runs` reads the shared ledger plus this checkout's and each sibling's local file;
  - a helper returns one run's events from the local files.
- `src/slicer/ops.py`:
  - `ledger_lock` and the relay-run writers catch `PermissionError`/`EPERM` on the shared path and fall back to the local file under `store.project_lock`;
  - `_open_run` searches every ledger;
  - `relay_run_end` copies the run's local events into the shared ledger before its end event, when the shared ledger is writable.
- `src/slicer/cli.py`: the stderr fallback line, and `end`'s text naming how many events it absorbed.
- `docs/commands.md` (Relay run ledger, sandboxes), `docs/agents.md`, the relay text in `src/slicer/ai.py` (one line on sandboxes), `CHANGELOG.md` under Fixed.
- `tests/test_relay_run.py`. Simulate the sandbox by making the fixture's own `<common>/slicer` directory read-only (`chmod 0o555`, inside TMPDIR), never the real repository.
